      "title": "Payment Gateway v2 Autoscaling and Rate Limiting Issues",
      "content_summary": "Resolving CPU spikes and rate limit errors when autoscaling fails to trigger. Covers capacity limitations and misconfigurations in the Rate Limiter.",
      "content_body": "If autoscaling does not trigger despite high CPU usage, check the Rate Limiter configuration for incorrect thresholds. A common cause is a capacity limitation in the underlying infrastructure that prevents new instances from spinning up. To resolve this, request a capacity increase from the infrastructure team. Alternatively, adjust the rate limit settings to align with the current capacity. If the infrastructure cannot scale, consider replacing the current setup with a more scalable architecture."
