      "title": "Webhook Engine Timeouts and Certificate Warnings",
      "content_summary": "Resolving connection refusals and timeout errors in webhook delivery. Addresses expired certificates and network configuration errors.",
      "content_body": "Timeouts and connection refused errors in the Webhook Engine are frequently caused by expired SSL certificates on the destination endpoint. Check the certificate validity and renew it if necessary. If certificates are valid, review the firewall rules to ensure they allow traffic from our IP ranges. Load balancer reconfiguration may also be needed if routing rules are misdirecting traffic. Always test connectivity with a simple curl request before diving deeper into application logs."
