      "title": "Handling Ambiguous Application Crash and Data Mismatch Reports",
      "content_summary": "Guidance for closing tickets with insufficient information or operator errors. Strategies for managing duplicate tickets and customer education.",
      "content_body": "When tickets lack sufficient information to determine a root cause, request detailed logs and reproduction steps from the customer. If the issue is clearly an operator error, provide documentation links and close the ticket with a note on customer education. For application crashes or data mismatches without clear cause, check for duplicate tickets before investing in deep investigation. If a duplicate is found, merge the tickets to consolidate communication. Otherwise, close the ticket as 'no action required' if the customer does not respond to requests for more data."
